# Bloodghast's landfall return is a "may": after Lightning Bolt kills it, Bot1 plays an Island on turn 3 and declines, so
# the Bloodghast stays in the graveyard (and Bot1's land is the only new permanent).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Bloodghast
Island
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodghast.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Bloodghast)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Bloodghast
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet; Island
